reconstructed research.md "8.1 webservice spike (T034)" (D-2 steps 1-5 ok, getNode a non-empty node name, clusterDownload of webservice.log without exception, exit 0) and the helper protocol (D-4, D-5).
Not recorded: frames written from the protocol with the fixed nonce, node name node1 and the byte count of ok.log; the log4j lines as in fixtures/queue-entry/v8_1/garbage_frames.frames. ok.log is a fictitious log of the shape the spike describes ("yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss,SSS <id> [WebService ...]" entries continued by HTTP request and response header blocks and SOAP bodies): acme services, partner.example.test, fictitious secrets in one Authorization: Basic header, one Set-Cookie header and one wsse:UsernameToken with one wsse:Password element. The text after "[WebService" and the entry ids are invented.
